      "claim": "Small polar/charged molecules acamprosate (~11%) and BMS-187745 (2.6%) provide transferable examples of low oral bioavailability.",
      "card_ids": ["C10", "C09"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C139", "C145"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for pyridostigmine in any supplied record.",
    "No matched oral versus IV exposure data for pyridostigmine.",
    "Neostigmine absorption record is from rat jejunum single-loop, not whole-intestinal or human F.",
    "Exact salt form/counterion is not specified.",
